> a(x: u8) = x^2
> equiv a ~ x*x
a and x*x are equal on the domain of a (exhaustive)
> b(x: u8) = ~(~(x^2))
  note: "^" between integers, next to bitwise operators: read as power, not xor (bitwise exclusive or) (write xor or ** to say which)
> equiv a b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (exhaustive)
> show b
b(x: u8) = x^2
  -> u8
